# Parallel Prefix Sum (Scan) in CUDA

## The Work-Efficient Algorithm: Blelloch Scan

The **Blelloch scan** (also called the "up-sweep/down-sweep" algorithm) is a work-efficient parallel prefix sum algorithm that runs in **O(n)** total work and **O(log n)** depth. It consists of two phases:

1. **Up-sweep (reduce phase)**: Build a binary tree by combining adjacent elements, moving from leaves to root.
2. **Down-sweep (broadcast phase)**: Propagate partial sums from the root back down to the leaves, computing the final prefix sums.

This is work-efficient because each element participates in exactly one operation per level, giving O(n) total operations across all threads, compared to the naive O(n log n) approach.

## CUDA Implementation

```cuda
#include <cuda_runtime.h>
#include <stdio.h>

/**
 * Work-efficient parallel prefix sum using Blelloch's up-sweep/down-sweep algorithm.
 * 
 * @param input  Input array of size n (must be power of 2)
 * @param output Output array of size n (prefix sum result)
 * @param n      Size of the array (must be a power of 2)
 */
__global__ void prefixSumKernel(const float* input, float* output, int n) {
    extern __shared__ float sdata[];

    int tid = threadIdx.x;
    int idx = tid;

    // Load input into shared memory
    if (idx < n) {
        sdata[tid] = input[idx];
    } else {
        sdata[tid] = 0.0f;  // Pad with zeros for non-power-of-2 sizes
    }
    __syncthreads();

    int offset = 1;

    // ---------------------------------------------------------
    // UP-SWEEP (reduce) phase: build the reduction tree
    // For each level, combine elements at distance 'offset'
    // ---------------------------------------------------------
    for (int d = n >> 1; d > 0; d >>= 1) {
        __syncthreads();
        if (tid < d) {
            int ai = offset * (2 * tid + 1) - 1;  // Right child index
            int bi = offset * (2 * tid + 2) - 1;  // Left child index
            sdata[bi] += sdata[ai];  // Accumulate into right child
        }
        offset *= 2;
    }

    // ---------------------------------------------------------
    // DOWN-SWEEP (broadcast) phase: propagate sums back down
    // ---------------------------------------------------------
    if (tid == 0) {
        sdata[n - 1] = 0.0f;  // Set root's contribution to 0 for exclusive scan
    }
    __syncthreads();

    for (int d = 1; d < n; d <<= 1) {
        offset >>= 1;
        __syncthreads();
        if (tid < d) {
            int ai = offset * (2 * tid + 1) - 1;  // Right child index
            int bi = offset * (2 * tid + 2) - 1;  // Left child index
            float t = sdata[ai];                  // Save left child value
            sdata[ai] = sdata[bi];                // Right child value goes to left
            sdata[bi] += t;                       // Left child value goes to right
        }
        __syncthreads();
    }

    // ---------------------------------------------------------
    // Write results back to global memory
    // ---------------------------------------------------------
    if (idx < n) {
        output[idx] = sdata[tid];
    }
}

